error[NK1314]: No shell is configured: `std` runs no shell (ADR-raw-sinks-1 D9).
  --> tests/process_shell.nika:8:5
   |
 8 |     let out = process::shell("echo hi; echo there | tr a-z A-Z")
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A shell reads its text as code, and a check of that text holds only for the one shell that reads it, so `std` starts none, on any platform.
   = help: Write the command as `process::run("PROGRAM", ["ARG", ...])`, whose arguments reach the program one by one and are never read as code.
